# audisp-strace: Enhancement Roadmap & To-Do List

## 1. Recently Completed Enhancements
• [x] Native Audit Log Follow Mode (`-F` / `--follow`, `--from-start`, `-n K`):
      Built-in rotation-aware live follower across inode changes, EOF sleeps, and truncations.
• [x] Unlinked-While-Open / "Ghost File" Tracking (`(deleted)`):
      Live `/proc/<pid>/fd/<fd>` inspection + offline cross-syscall tracking decorating deleted open files across read/write/close.
• [x] Audit Sequence Gap & Drop Detection (`-g` / `--detect-drops`, `--drop-threshold`, `--drop-window`):
      Sliding-window netlink jitter absorption, idle flush timeout, warning banners, JSON drop events, and summary metrics.
• [x] Mount & Filesystem Namespace Syscall Class (`%mount` / `%mounts` / `%mnt`):
      19 mount, filesystem namespace, and container isolation syscalls (mount, umount2, pivot_root, chroot, new Mount API, unshare, setns, swapon/swapoff).
• [x] File & Record Locking Syscall Class (`%locks` / `%lock`):
      `flock` and `fcntl` with `F_SETLK`/`F_SETLKW`/`F_GETLK`, 64-bit variants, and Open File Description `F_OFD_*` locks with sub-command filtering and `{...}` formatting.
• [x] Targeted Error Code Filtering (`-e` / `--errno`, `-E` / `--exclude-errno`):
      Filter or exclude specific error names (e.g. `EACCES`, `ENOENT`, `EPERM`) or numeric error codes (`13`, `2`), case-insensitive and prefixless (`acces`, `13`). Implies failed-only for `-e`; fully integrated with summary mode (`-c`) and JSON output (`--json`).
• [x] Output Stream & File Compression (`--compress`, `-o <file>.gz`, `--gzip`, `--compress-level`):
      Transparently compresses output traces, JSON records, and summary tables with gzip, bz2, or xz. Auto-detected by filename extension on `-o` or explicitly selected via `--compress`. Uses fast default `compresslevel=1` for ~90-95% compression with minimal CPU overhead, deterministic flushing for real-time `zcat`/`zless` visibility, clean RFC 1952 concatenated stream support with `-A` / `--append`, terminal protection check for stdout, and transparent decompression of compressed audit input logs.
• [x] Conversion of File/Directory Mode Bits to Readable Format (`0755 <rwxr-xr-x>`):
      Decodes octal mode arguments across `chmod`, `fchmod`, `fchmodat`, `open`, `openat`, `creat`, `mkdir`, `mkdirat`, `mknod`, `mknodat`, and `umask` (both mask parameter and previous mask return value) with readable symbolic permissions (`0755 <rwxr-xr-x>`, `0644 <rw-r--r-->`, `04755 <rwsr-xr-x>`, `02755 <rwxr-sr-x>`, `01777 <rwxrwxrwt>`, `0022 <----w--w->`, `0 <--------->`). Automatically decodes file type flags in `mknod` (`S_IFIFO|0644 <rw-r--r-->`) and properly isolates System V IPC flags in `shmget`/`semget`/`msgget` (`IPC_CREAT|0600`).
• [x] Multi-File Rotated Log Chronological Merging (`-m` / `--merge`, `--sort-time`, `--chronological`):
      Performs an $O(\log K)$ memory-efficient k-way chronological merge of audit events across multiple input files using `heapq.merge` based on timestamp and serial number. Seamlessly handles rotated log segments passed in reverse/arbitrary order, cluster logs, and mixed compression formats (`.gz`, `.bz2`, `.xz`).
• [x] Relative Timestamps (`-r` / `--relative-time` / `--relative-timestamps`, `-t relative`, `--relative-by-pid`):
      Displays elapsed time deltas since previous events modeled after `strace -r` with microsecond precision. Standard `-r` appends relative deltas (`(+     0.001253)`) next to wall-clock timestamps (`-t time`, `-t datetime`, `-t epoch`), while `-t relative` renders standalone deltas (`     0.001253`). Optional `--relative-by-pid` isolates deltas per process rather than across the global stream. Seamlessly integrated with compact modes (`-C`, `-C strace`), JSON export (`"relative_time": 0.001253`), and multi-file merging (`-m`).
• [x] Fast Log Time Range Inspection & Summary Boundaries (`--time-range`, `-c` / `--summary`):
      Provides instant (<1ms) metadata inspection of audit log files via seek-based header/trailer reads on uncompressed files and streaming fallback on compressed files (`.gz`, `.bz2`, `.xz`) or stdin. Displays start/end timestamps, human-readable duration, and serial ranges per file, with multi-file alignment and an overall Total span line. Enriches summary mode (`-c` / `--summary`) to display the matched event time range and duration header above the syscall frequency table.
• [x] Audit Rule Generator (`--generate-rules` / `--auditctl` / `--rules`, `--rule-key`, `--rules-format`, `--arch`):
      Translates active CLI filters (`-s`, `%CLASS`, `-P`, `-u`, `--auid`, `-p`, `--exe`, `-Z`, `-z`) into exact, ready-to-run `auditctl` shell scripts or `/etc/audit/rules.d/` rule files. Automatically chunks syscalls into safe kernel batches, applies `-F arch=b64` (or `--arch both`/`b32`), resolves usernames to UIDs, formats directory/file path filters (`-F dir=` vs `-F path=`), inserts self-session loop prevention (`-a never,exit -F sessionid=...`), and outputs rule teardown/cleanup commands.

---

## 2. High-Value Enhancement Suggestions & Remaining To-Do Items

### A. Security & Anomaly Detection
• Security & Anomaly Highlighting (Heuristic Flags / Badges):
    • What it does: Optional visual badges/alerts or filters for suspicious filesystem security anomalies:
        • Creation of SUID/SGID binaries (`chmod 4755` or `chmod +s`).
        • Execution from world-writable or temporary directories (`/tmp`, `/dev/shm`, `/var/tmp`).
        • Modification of critical system files (`/etc/ld.so.preload`, `/etc/shadow`, `/etc/sudoers`, `/etc/pam.d/*`).
    • Support Value: Medium. Highlights potential privilege escalation or tampering attempts.

### D. Packaging & Deployment
• `make install` / Packaging Target:
    • What it does: Simple Makefile install target to install `audisp-strace` to `/usr/local/bin` (or `/usr/bin`) and install `audisp-strace.conf` into `/etc/audit/plugins.d/` (or `/etc/audisp/plugins.d/` depending on distro release).
    • Support Value: Convenience for server deployment.
